{"id":"01M645KCMGQ39KN9S1NZQ06EHG","seq":30,"ts":"2026-10-29T15:49:02.224Z","task":"T-0003","run":"r1","adapter":"muse-code","vendor":"meta","type":"agent.message","payload":{"text":"Done. `clamp(value, min, max)` is implemented, documented, and both suites pass with 100% coverage (190 tests, observed locally; the daemon's run is the record).\n\ndecision: clamp reuses the shared toMilliseconds helper, parameterized with the caller name so its errors say clamp() while add()'s messages are unchanged\ndecision: clamp is Math.min(Math.max(value, min), max) with no min<=max validation; inverted bounds yield max\n\nWhat changed:\n\n- [src/index.ts](<clone>/.stint/worktrees/T-0003-r1/src/index.ts) - exported `clamp(value, min, max)`, each arg a duration string or ms number, returning ms held in `[min, max]`. Throws for non-string/non-finite inputs, matching `add`/`toSeconds` conventions. The private `toMilliseconds` helper gained a caller-name parameter; `add` behavior is unchanged.\n- [src/clamp.test.ts](<clone>/.stint/worktrees/T-0003-r1/src/clamp.test.ts) - new test file covering the three acceptance cases (`clamp('2h','1m','1h')` → 3600000, `clamp('30s','1m','1h')` → 60000, `clamp(90000,'1m','1h')` → 90000), boundary equality, all-number/all-string args, negatives, and error cases.\n- [README.md](<clone>/.stint/worktrees/T-0003-r1/README.md) - new \"Clamp Durations\" section with the acceptance examples.\n\nVerification observed: `typecheck` and `lint` clean; `test:nodejs` 7 suites / 190 tests pass at 100% stmts/branch/funcs/lines; `test:edge` 7 suites / 190 tests pass. No locked test files were modified.\n\nWhat I did not do: the `stint` CLI isn't installed here, so I couldn't read the T-0002 packet; I derived the contract from the `add`/`toSeconds` code and tests in the tree instea..."},"raw":{"kind":"transcript","pointer":"r1/transcript.jsonl#318636","byteLen":2698,"redacted":false},"prev":"d685644b265990a859c2d10887952eb32a76102527443dd0ad97531983750550","hash":"45